cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite the original SpeedCHEM methods paper and identify the exact
  repository revision used in your work.
title: "SpeedCHEM: community-maintained Fortran chemical-kinetics library"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Perini
    given-names: Federico
  - name: GTT10 contributors
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/GTT10/sppedchem"
url: "https://www.federicoperini.info/speedchem"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  SpeedCHEM is a Fortran library for stiff gas-phase chemical kinetics using
  sparse analytical Jacobians. This repository maintains and extends the
  original SpeedCHEM source for current research workflows.
keywords:
  - chemical kinetics
  - combustion
  - sparse Jacobian
  - Fortran
  - PLOG
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: Perini
      given-names: Federico
    - family-names: Galligani
      given-names: Emanuele
    - family-names: Reitz
      given-names: Rolf D.
  title: >-
    An Analytical Jacobian Approach to Sparse Reaction Kinetics for
    Computationally Efficient Combustion Modeling with Large Reaction
    Mechanisms
  journal: Energy & Fuels
  year: 2012
  volume: 26
  issue: 8
  start: 4804
  end: 4822
  doi: 10.1021/ef300747n
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Perini
        given-names: Federico
      - family-names: Galligani
        given-names: Emanuele
      - family-names: Reitz
        given-names: Rolf D.
    title: >-
      A Study of Direct and Krylov Iterative Sparse Solver Techniques to
      Approach Linear Scaling of the Integration of Chemical Kinetics with
